instead of `-$3.10`. It now formats the absolute value and adds the `-` sign in front, so `-5` gives `-$0.05`.\n2. **`ledger/parse.py` – `parse_date`:** month and day were swapped in the returned tuple. It now returns `(year, month, day)`. This also fixed `parse_record`.\n3. **`ledger/report.py` – `top_items`:** items were sorted by total from smallest to largest, with no tie-breaking. They're now sorted by total from largest to smallest, and equal totals are ordered by item name A to Z. This also fixed `summary_line`.\n\nI also tried a few documented cases the visible tests don't cover, and all came out right: `format_cents(-5)` gives `-$0.05`, `format_cents(0)` gives `$0.00`, `parse_amount(\"0.5\")` gives 50, and two items with the same total are ordered by name.","ttft_ms":2243,"type":"result","duration_ms":15851,"uuid":"3c6c1cbc-99e4-45b9-872b-017cb09e1526","ttft_stream_ms":741,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":741,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
